; Evaluation is f64 and the ONE narrowing to f32 happens at write-buffer
; encode — so a value that does not fit f32 would land as ±inf. The
; `(repr-shape :type f32)` on the kinds that narrow refuses it at
; compile, and BOTH spellings of the slot now say so: `:value` is typed
; by the `key-value` union, `:t` by the bare `stage-weight`, and each
; records repr_out_of_range on the offending literal.
;
; The union used to swallow it — `union_no_branch_matched` named the two
; alternatives and no branch's private cause — until SJON gave every
; shape-disjoint union the arm rule (filed from here as SJON ask 15,
; built 2026-08-26). A number can only have meant `plain-number`, so
; that arm's own diagnostic is what the slot reports.
(transport :bpm 120)

(track :target radius
  (key :at 0b :value 1e39)
  (key :at 1b :value 1 :ease (seq (stage :ease linear :t 1e39 :v 1))))
